<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnSegmentsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">5. Directorate of Enforcement, Zonal Office, Ahmedabad (ED) has conducted search at the Corporate Office &amp; factory of the Company situated at Palodia &amp; the residence of Mr.Shailesh Bhandari, Executive Vice Chairman (EVC) &amp; Promoter of the Company on 10-01-2025 under the provisions of Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 (PMLA) &amp; made following orders under Section 17(1A) of the PMLA, 2002: (i) For freezing of the balances lying in 39 bank accounts of the Company along with interest accrued thereon as on 10-01-2025 &amp; the interest accrued subsequently from 10-01-2025 onwards;  (ii) For freezing of balances lying in the two personal bank accounts of Mr. Shailesh Bhandari, EVC, along with interest accrued thereon as on 11-01-2025 &amp; (iii) Seized two cars found at the residence premises of Mr. Shailesh Bhandari, EVC. Proceedings under PMLA, 2002 is initiated in connection with FIR registered by Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI), Banking Securities &amp; Fraud Branch, Mumbai against the company &amp; its directors based on the complaint of Bank of India in December,2021 for causing loss of Rs.81.97 Crores to Bank of India, being the difference amount between the outstanding dues of Rs.631.97 Crores &amp; assignment of loan by Bank of India to Edelweiss Asset Reconstruction Company Limited on 30-06-2014 for Rs.550.00Crores. The FIR registered by CBI has already been disclosed in the financial statements/annual reports ended as on 31-03-2022 onwards. The Company &amp; Mr. Shailesh Bhandari has filed a petition for quashing of CBI FIR before Hon’ble Gujarat High Court in April 2024 &amp; Hon’ble Gujarat High Court by order dated 26-04-2024 issued notice &amp; notice as to interim relief. Further, the Company &amp; Mr. Shailesh Bhandari, EVC challenged the actions of ED dated 10th/11th January 2025 before the Hon’ble Gujarat High Court &amp; the Hon’ble Gujarat High Court by interim order dated 29-01-2025, till the pendency of the said petitions, inter alia, permitted the Company to operate the bank accounts as mentioned in the order of ED dated 10-01-2025 in respect of the amount which is in excess of amount freezed to the tune of approx. Rs.33.67 Crores (amount revised to Rs.34.29 Crores) by ED on 10-01-2025 &amp; permitted Mr. Shailesh Bhandari, Executive Vice Chairman to operate the bank accounts as mentioned in the order of ED dated 11-01-2025 in respect of the amount which is in excess of the amount freezed to the tune of approx. Rs.0.83 Crores by ED on 11-01-2025,. The said petitions are pending for further hearing before Hon’ble Gujarat High Court. ED through email dated 05-02-2025 directed the Axis bank to mark the lien for Rs34.29 Crores in two bank account with them and allow operation over &amp; above the lien amount. ED further directed that other Bank accounts are hereby completely de-freeze &amp; are allowed to be operated. The company is in process of ascertaining any further impact on the financial statement on account of the search &amp; would account it accordingly. 6.ET-Elec Trans Limited (subsidiarycompany) has incurred cash loss of Rs.0.00Crore &amp; accumulated losses of Rs1.49Crore which has fully eroded the net worth &amp; was non-operative. In view of negative networth &amp; not in operation, The company has sold 7,24,400 equity share of ET-Elec Trans Limited to Mr. ChaitanyaPratap Sharma (Independent Director/a Non-Executive Director of Subsidiary Company &amp; Joint Venture) for Rs.0.10/- per equity sharei.e. total consideration for transfer of Equity Shares is Rs.0.01Crore on 13-11-2024 (now ceases to be a subsidiary company). Since April2016 the company has already provided for Impairment in value of Investment in ET-Elec Trans Limited for Rs0.72Crore. Further during the Quarter ended on 31-12-2024, trade receivable due from ET-Elec Trans Limited of Rs0.51Crore has been written off on which Provision for Expected Credit Loss has already been provided since April2016. Remaining note no. 7 &amp; 8 are referred from the Outcome of the Board Meeting dated 11-02-2025.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnSegmentsExplanatoryTextBlock>
